# Returns the folder chain pClassRef sits in, as NAMES joined by /, and the
# empty string for a class on the top level.
#
# NAMES and not idents: an ident is only valid inside the library that issued
# it, and the index is read in a different library than the one it describes.
#
# The walk is the one $ensureFolder does on the vault side. It is repeated
# here rather than shared, because $ensureFolder needs the chain innermost
# first in order to create it, and this needs it outermost first in order to
# print it. Sharing would mean one of the two turning its own list around.
#
# $parentfolder comes back EMPTY for top level, not 0 - hence the isclear.

If isclear(pClassRef)
	Quit method ''
End If
If pClassRef.$classtype*1=kFolder*1
	Calculate id as pClassRef.$ident
Else
	Calculate id as pClassRef.$parentfolder
End If
If isclear(id)
	Quit method ''
End If
Set reference libRef to pClassRef.$lib().$ref
If isclear(libRef)
	Quit method ''
End If

Calculate text as ''
Calculate guard as 0
While id<>0
	Calculate guard as guard+1
	If guard>50
		Break to end of loop
	End If
	Set reference fRef to libRef.$classes.$findident(id)
	If isclear(fRef)
		Calculate id as 0
	Else
		Calculate text as pick(len(text)=0,con(fRef.$name,'/',text),fRef.$name)
		Calculate id as fRef.$parentfolder
		If isclear(id)
			Calculate id as 0
		End If
	End If
End While
Quit method text